WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.349
A simple gesture. A new cycle.

2
00:00:02.349 --> 00:00:06.911
Meet EcoNova, a concept designed to make recycling feel effortless.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.423
Scan the station’s code to begin.

4
00:00:10.423 --> 00:00:13.169
A future app would confirm your session on site,

5
00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:14.996
ready for a verified deposit.

6
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.349
Plastic bottles, cans, and accepted paper share one opening.

7
00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:25.342
Local collection rules guide every deposit:

8
00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:27.407
no liquids or hazardous waste.

9
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.080
Inside, a separator would present each object on its own,

10
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.167
giving the sensors a clear view while checking for jams.

11
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.728
Light, cameras, and additional sensors would help identify the material.

12
00:00:43.728 --> 00:00:45.461
When confidence is low,

13
00:00:45.461 --> 00:00:47.745
EcoNova would hold the item for review.

14
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.141
Plastic bottles slide to the left.

15
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.949
Cans fall through the central hatch.

16
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.992
Paper follows the plate to the right.

17
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.845
Uncertain items enter a separate holding bay.

18
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.735
Only a verified deposit would add EcoPoints to your app.

19
00:01:05.735 --> 00:01:07.721
One deposit, one credit;

20
00:01:07.721 --> 00:01:09.721
this wallet is a demonstration.

21
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.992
Separate compartments keep materials apart.

22
00:01:14.992 --> 00:01:17.996
Accessible modules support cleaning and repair.

23
00:01:17.996 --> 00:01:22.857
A pilot would measure sorting accuracy, energy, cost, and reliability.

24
00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.334
Our mission: make recycling simpler,

25
00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.051
then prove the impact.

26
00:01:27.051 --> 00:01:32.000
Next comes a prototype, and results everyone can inspect.
